{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.braidAction_not_injective_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.braidAction_not_injective_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.lean#L184-L191","doc":"`IsUnit q` is load-bearing in `braidAction_injective`: drop it and the\nstatement is false, witnessed at `q = 0` on strand `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.zeroQCounterModel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.zeroQCounterModel","kind":"def","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.lean#L158-L182","doc":"**Counter-model at `q = 0`** — a `def`, never an `instance`.\n\nOver `R = ℤ` at `q = 0`, with normal forms `ℤ` and the action that negates\non strand `0` and kills every other strand, all three fields hold. It exists\nfor two reasons, and neither is to discharge the conjecture.\n\n1. It proves the `IsUnit q` hypothesis of `braidAction_injective` is\n   load-bearing (`braidAction_not_injective_at_zero` below), so that theorem\n   says something about `q` rather than holding for free.\n2. It makes concrete what the class does **not** settle: an instance exists,\n   so *possessing* one is not evidence for `conj:hecke-anyonic-substrate`.\n   See the scope note below for why, and what would change it.\n\nPer AGENTS.md §3b-tax this is deliberately **not** an `instance` — a global\ninstance would silently discharge every `[HeckeAnyonicSubstrate R q]`\nhypothesis in the tree. Same disposition as\n`KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit.canonical`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.normal_form_inhabited_of_action","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.normal_form_inhabited_of_action","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.lean#L147-L156","doc":"Trivial unconditional fact: the predicate `anyonic_holds` is\npropositional and therefore `Subsingleton`-like — two proofs of\nthe same existential agree as Props.  This is a scaffolding lemma\nshowing the class can be used unconditionally to extract data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.braidAction_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.braidAction_injective","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.lean#L114-L144","doc":"**The quadratic relation, consumed.** At any `q` that is a unit, every braid\ngenerator acts *injectively* on normal forms.\n\nThis is the first declaration in the corpus to read `heckeQuadratic`, and it\nis why the field is worth encoding: `(T_i - q)(T_i + 1) = 0` rearranges to\n`T_i (T_i - (q - 1)) = q`, so `q • -` factors through `braidAction i` and\ninjectivity follows from `q` being cancellable. No linearity of\n`braidAction` is needed, and none is assumed — only the relation itself.\n\n**It can fail, which is the point.** The `IsUnit q` hypothesis is\nload-bearing rather than decorative: at `q = 0` the relation reads\n`T_i^2 = -T_i`, which the zero action satisfies on any module, so the\nconclusion is false there for any `NormalForm` with more than one element.\nA statement that survived every `q` would be saying nothing about `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.anyonic_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.anyonic_holds","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.lean#L107-L107","doc":"**The conjecture itself**: every QOU particle's normal form\nlies in the image of the braid action.  This field plays the\nrole of `sorry` for `conj:hecke-anyonic-substrate`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.heckeQuadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.heckeQuadratic","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.lean#L102-L102","doc":"The Hecke quadratic relation `(T_{s_i} - q)(T_{s_i} + 1) = 0`, in the\nequivalent acted-on form `T_i^2 = (q - 1) T_i + q`.\n\n**Transcribed from the block's own displayed equation** (2026-09-14).\n`hecke-anyonic-substrate.md` states the relation as\n`(T_{s_i} - q)(T_{s_i} + 1) = 0`; expanding gives\n`T^2 + (1 - q) T - q = 0`, i.e. `T^2 = (q - 1) T + q`, and applying that\nto a normal form `T` is the field below. Nothing here is chosen: the\nformula is the block's, and a reviewer checks this line against the `.md`\nrather than against any reasoning of mine.\n\n**What it replaces.** The field used to read `heckeQuadratic : Prop` — a\nfield typed with the *universe* `Prop`, so the instance supplied a\nproposition rather than a proof of one and `True` was a legal choice. Its\nown docstring recorded that the relation was held \"abstractly as a Prop\nthe concrete instance supplies\", that nothing read it, and that encoding\nit \"means giving `NormalForm` the algebra structure first\". That last\nsentence is the fix, and it is cheap: `NormalForm` now carries\n`AddCommGroup` and `Module R` as instance fields, which is *weaker* than\nwhat the block already asserts (it places `T_w` in the algebra\n`H_n(R, q)`), so requiring a module structure adds no claim.\n\nThe relation is now **consumed**: `braidAction_injective` below derives\nfrom it that every braid generator acts injectively whenever `q` is a\nunit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.braidAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.braidAction","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.lean#L76-L76","doc":"Action of the `i`-th braid generator on a normal form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.isModule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.isModule","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.lean#L74-L74","doc":"... and its `R`-module structure, which is what lets the quadratic\nrelation be written down at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.addCommGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.addCommGroup","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.lean#L71-L71","doc":"`T_w` are elements of the algebra `H_n(R, q)`, so normal forms carry\nits additive structure. Instance field: see `heckeQuadratic`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.NormalForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.NormalForm","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.lean#L68-L68","doc":"Abstract type of Hecke normal forms `T_w ∈ H_n(R, q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.mk","kind":"ctor","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAnyonicSubstrate","kind":"class","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeAnyonicSubstrate.lean#L47-L108","doc":"**Hecke anyonic substrate (conjecture).**\n\nThe `class` axiomatises that every QOU particle is an anyon at\ngeneric `q`: its topological statistics are governed by the\nbraid-group action on a normal form `T : NormalForm` through the\nHecke surjection.\n\nThe fields encode:\n- `braidAction` — the action of generator `i` on a normal form;\n- `heckeQuadratic` — the defining relation\n  `(σ_i - q) ∘ (σ_i + 1) = 0`;\n- `anyonic_holds` — the **conjectural** statement that the QOU\n  particle spectrum is exhausted by `H_n(R, q)`-modules. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:hecke-anyonic-substrate","label":"conj:hecke-anyonic-substrate","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/hecke-anyonic-substrate.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}